{"judge_label": "committed_silent", "justification_span": "Given: male, age 66, creatinine 1.7 mg/dl.\n\n2021 CKD-EPI (no race) for males:\n- If Scr ≤ 0.9: eGFR = 142 × (Scr/0.9)^(-0.302) × 0.9938^age\n- If Scr > 0.9: eGFR = 142 × (Scr/0.9)^(-1.200) × 0.9938^age\n\nScr = 1.7 > 0.9, so use exponent -1.200.\n\nScr/0.9 = 1.7/0.9 = 1.8889\n\n(1.8889)^(-1.200):\nln(1.8889) = 0.6360\n× -1.200 = -0.7632\ne^(-0.7632) = 0.4662\n\n0.9938^66:\nln(0.9938) = -0.006219\n× 66 = -0.4105\ne^(-0.4105) = 0.6633\n\neGFR = 142 × 0.4662 × 0.6633\n= 142 × 0.30923\n= 43.9\n\nFINAL: 43.9"}